meta {
  name: Rename Library Video
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/virtual/videos/{{virtualVideoId}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": "Tango básico - clase 1"
  }
}

docs {
  #841, ADR-0049. Renames a video in the Bunny Stream library (Bunny updates with POST; this API exposes PUT).
  {{virtualVideoId}} is the guid of a video: run "List Library Videos" first (it stores the first one) or set it.

  ADMIN renames any video of the library; INSTRUCTOR only a video used by a lesson of their own courses
  (403 VIDEO_NOT_OWNED otherwise, also when no lesson uses it). title: not blank, at most 255 characters, trimmed.
  Only the title changes in Bunny; lessons keep the videoId. A RENAME_VIDEO audit row is written.

  Against a local API (demo / e2e profiles, or without APP_CDN_BUNNYNET_APIKEY) the library is the in-memory
  double and starts empty, so a rename answers 404 until a video exists. Against a real library use a TEST
  library, never production (see the ADR-0049 follow-up note).

  Success contract: 200 with VirtualVideoResponse (the video with its new title and the lessons the actor may see).
  Error contract:
    400 INVALID_REQUEST           → blank, missing or too long title; videoId that is not a plain identifier
    401 AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED   → no token
    403 VIDEO_NOT_OWNED           → INSTRUCTOR and no lesson of their own courses uses the video
    403 ACCESS_DENIED             → neither ADMIN nor INSTRUCTOR
    404 VIDEO_NOT_FOUND           → the library has no such video
    503 VIDEO_LIBRARY_UNAVAILABLE → Bunny did not answer (timeout, error or rejected key)
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.videoId: eq {{virtualVideoId}}
  res.body.title: eq Tango básico - clase 1
  res.body.lessons: isArray
}
